Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: mgmt_tx without a channel uses the current one

WPA3-Personal goes through external auth: the driver asks wpa_supplicant
to run SAE, and wpa_supplicant sends the commit and confirm frames with
NL80211_CMD_FRAME and no frequency (freq=0).  mgmt_tx refused any frame
without a channel with -EINVAL, so the commit never left and every SAE
connection timed out after the driver's 8 s wait.

The driver is already on the AP's channel at that point; when no channel
is given, transmit on the operating channel.
---
--- a/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
@@ -8074,13 +8074,14 @@
 	wdev = ndev_to_wdev(ndev);
 #endif
 
-	if (chan == NULL) {
-		ret = -EINVAL;
-		goto exit;
-	}
-
 	rfctl = adapter_to_rfctl(padapter);
-	tx_ch = (u8)ieee80211_frequency_to_channel(chan->center_freq);
+	/* No channel given: wpa_supplicant sends the SAE commit/confirm of
+	 * an external auth that way, while we already sit on the AP's
+	 * channel; use the one we are on. */
+	if (chan)
+		tx_ch = (u8)ieee80211_frequency_to_channel(chan->center_freq);
+	else
+		tx_ch = rtw_get_oper_ch(padapter);
 	if (IS_CH_WAITING(rfctl)) {
 		#ifdef CONFIG_DFS_MASTER
 		if (_rtw_rfctl_overlap_radar_detect_ch(rfctl, tx_ch, CHANNEL_WIDTH_20, HAL_PRIME_CHNL_OFFSET_DONT_CARE)) {
